 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids January to February came in under 90% of normal in 41 of them. On the middle of the grids in 2025, January to February ran 52% of normal and February to March 56%, then August to September hit 159%. So far in 2026, March to April on the middle of the grids came in at 9% of normal. Grid 22015 had its driest year in 1956 at 43%.</p>"}
